🚀 Let's Go to the Azure Portal! (Scenario 1)
Maza toh tab aayega jab hum is Git ki speed ko Azure Cloud ke sath jodenge. Chaliye shuru karte hain Scenario 1: Same Tenant - Same Subscription - Same Region.

Hamara goal hai: Do alag VNets banana, unke beech Peering karna, aur connectivity test karna.

🛠️ Step 1: Create Two VNets (Do Networks Banayein)
Apne Azure Portal (portal.azure.com) par login kariye aur ye do VNets banayein. IP ranges ka dhyan rakhna, overlap nahi hona chahiye!

VNet 1: (Name: Hub-VNet)
Resource Group: Ek naya banayein, naam rakhein RG-Networking-Lab.

Region: Select karein East US.

IP Address Space (CIDR): 10.1.0.0/16

Subnet Name: Subnet-A (Range: 10.1.1.0/24)

VNet 2: (Name: Spoke-VNet)
Resource Group: Same select karein RG-Networking-Lab.

Region: Same select karein East US (Kyunki hum same region test kar rahe hain).

IP Address Space (CIDR): 10.2.0.0/16 (Dekhiye, yeh 10.1 se alag hai, yani non-overlapping).

Subnet Name: Subnet-B (Range: 10.2.1.0/24)

🛠️ Step 2: Deploy Virtual Machines (VMs)
Dono networks me ek-ek choti test machine (VM) banayein taaki connectivity check kar sakein.

VM-1 (Hub-VM): Ise Hub-VNet ke Subnet-A me deploy karein. Size me sabse sasta wala (B1s ya B1ls) select karna taaki free credits bachein.

VM-2 (Spoke-VM): Ise Spoke-VNet ke Subnet-B me deploy karein. Same sasta size.

(Pro-Tip: Dono VMs ka username aur password same rakhna taaki yaad rakhne me aasani ho).

🛠️ Step 3: Enable VNet Peering
Jab dono VMs ready (Running state me) ho jayein:

Portal me Hub-VNet par jaiye.

Left side menu me Settings ke andar Peerings par click kariye.

+ Add button par click kariye.

Ek form khulega, use is tarah bhariye:

Peering link name (This VNet): Hub-to-Spoke

Peering link name (Remote VNet): Spoke-to-Hub

Virtual Network: Dropdown se Spoke-VNet select kar lijiye.

Baaki saari settings ko default (Allow) rehne dein aur neeche Add par click kar dein.

Azure dono taraf se automatic link status "Connected" kar dega (Agle 30 seconds me).